{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21086-demonic-form-questions","id":21086,"title":"Demonic form questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-01T03:10:30-08:00","id":21086,"title":"Demonic form questions","content":"I've read a few times through the demonic forms and I'm unsure of how to best simulate something like a grapling tail.<br /> The &quot;modification&quot; with the barbed tail is &quot;just&quot; a pincer from what I read. Thus feelingwise &quot;extra limbs&quot; would best accomodate to a grappling tail rulewise.<br /> Or am I wrong there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T03:18:47-08:00","id":21092,"title":"","content":"Tether I think simulates a grappling tail pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T03:37:36-08:00","id":21098,"title":"","content":"not so sure as tether doesn't allow fine manipulation or so only movement by tail which isn't what I had in mind there. more something like a succubus tail (non poisonous and non pincer) or a cats tail. Thus into that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T05:30:27-08:00","id":21125,"title":"","content":"An additional question here, as the build clairvoyant sight + teleport was mentioned a few times.<br /> Is it so that teleporting by using clairvoyant sight gains the user the captivated condition? Or is that not so because teleport is reflexive and thus does not break the concentration?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Additionally inhuman reflexes, inhuman strength.<br /> Does inhuman reflexes also add to derived stats like initiative and defense (example wits 4, dex 2 char who has inhuman reflexes)?<br /> Does inhuman strength add to the damage of attacks?<br /> <br /> Additional Edit:<br /> Goind loud: As that raises primum temporarily, does it also unlock demonic form abilities or give the ability to change the current abilities (as with normal primum gains)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","user":"Ryu","date":". 12-01-2013, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T07:36:23-08:00","id":21151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An additional question here, as the build clairvoyant sight + teleport was mentioned a few times.<br /> Is it so that teleporting by using clairvoyant sight gains the user the captivated condition? Or is that not so because teleport is reflexive and thus does not break the concentration? </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally inhuman reflexes, inhuman strength.<br /> Does inhuman reflexes also add to derived stats like initiative and defense (example wits 4, dex 2 char who has inhuman reflexes)? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does inhuman strength add to the damage of attacks? </div> </div> </div>Damage? no. It adds dies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Goind loud: As that raises primum temporarily, does it also unlock demonic form abilities or give the ability to change the current abilities (as with normal primum gains)? </div> </div> </div>No, you don't sprout demonic forms that fall off when you go loud.<br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> Here's a question of my own. Under <b>Causes of Compromise </b>(pg159) assuming Demonic Form is listed as a -3 compromise roll. Under <b>Demonic Form - Full Transformation </b>(pg296) the compromise roll is listed as -2. Which one is it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T07:44:07-08:00","id":21152,"title":"","content":"&quot;Does inhuman strength add to the damage of attacks? Damage? no. It adds dies.&quot;<br /> that is the strange thing, the close combat build in the book has that form power (dont know why then though)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T07:47:46-08:00","id":21154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21086-demonic-form-questions?p=21152#post21152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Does inhuman strength add to the damage of attacks? Damage? no. It adds dies.&quot;<br /> that is the strange thing, the close combat build in the book has that form power (dont know why then though)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Because the to-hit roll is still Strength-based and rolling more successes to hit still translates to more damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T08:27:29-08:00","id":21159,"title":"","content":"ah there was the error in thinking I had^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}